to contend that at interlocutory stage, trial Court should not conduct mini-trial or finally adjudicate disputed questions.
Learned counsel argued that trial Court duly considered prima facie case,
balance of convenience and risk of irreparable harm likely to be suffered and arriving at conclusion that same favoured plaintiff given its longstanding registration and goodwill built up, granted orders of temporary injunction as prayed.
Therefore, same did not call for interference.
